<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Comparison of image classification results on the ImageNet-1K dataset. Tp. (images/s) is measured on a single 4090 GPU with batch size 256.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Sx5.p30" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx5.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx5.p30.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Complexity Analysis. </span>Let <math id="Sx5.p30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> denote the number of channels, and <math id="Sx5.p30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> denote the size of the convolution kernel. The computational cost of calculating <math id="Sx5.p30.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx5.p30.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx5.p30.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx5.p30.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\_gate" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\_gate</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx5.p30.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\_gate" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\_gate</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Sx5.p30.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and outputs projections is <math id="Sx5.p30.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7Nd^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7Nd^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The Hadamard-product of <math id="Sx5.p30.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K,K\_gate)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K,K\_gate)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx5.p30.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V,V\_gate)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V,V\_gate)</annotation></semantics></math> has a computational cost of <math id="Sx5.p30.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2Nd" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2Nd</annotation></semantics></math>. The attention computation for <math id="Sx5.p30.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Q,K,V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Q,K,V)</annotation></semantics></math> requires a computational cost of <math id="Sx5.p30.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2Nd^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2Nd^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The convolution operation requires <math id="Sx5.p30.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{2}Nd" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{2}Nd</annotation></semantics></math>. The computational cost required for output augment <math id="Sx5.p30.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Sx5.p30.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Nd" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Nd</annotation></semantics></math>. In summary, the total complexity of SAGA is given by Eq.(<a href="#Sx5.E11" title="In Method ‣ SAGA: Selective Adaptive Gating for Efficient and Expressive Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), and it exhibits linear complexity with respect to <math id="Sx5.p30.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx5.p31" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx5.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx5.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta=9N{d^{2}}+{k^{2}}Nd+3Nd" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta=9N{d^{2}}+{k^{2}}Nd+3Nd</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
